# Never translate line endings, in either direction.
#
# The device clones this repo and executes update.sh, run.sh and
# startblake2b.sh directly. A CRLF checkout would put a \r on the end of the
# shebang, and the kernel would fail the exec with a "bad interpreter" error
# naming a path that looks completely correct. There is no SSH to this device,
# so that failure would be close to undiagnosable. The device's git config is
# not ours to control, hence pinning it here rather than relying on the default.
* -text
